jobs.description:
In this position, you will be responsible for assembling, connecting, and maintaining industrial electrical systems. You will work with power distribution systems, cable routes, control panels, and industrial machinery. Together with your team, you ensure that installations operate safely and efficiently.

Your tasks include:

- Installing and connecting industrial electrical equipment;
- Reading electrical diagrams and technical documentation;
- Troubleshooting and repairing electrical malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations and carrying out maintenance work;
- Working together with colleagues and supervisors on-site.

- Completed MBO education in Electrical Engineering;
- Experience in industrial electrical work;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain it;
- Knowledge of NEN 1010 and NEN 3140 is a plus;
- Independent and accurate working attitude;
- Dutch or English speaking.

As a Maritime Electrical Technician, you will work on the installation, maintenance, and repair of electrical systems on different types of vessels, including yachts, offshore vessels, and workboats. You will be involved in projects ranging from new shipbuilding to maintenance and refit activities.

Your responsibilities include:

- Reading and interpreting maritime electrical drawings and schematics;
- Installing onboard cabling, switchboards, and control systems;
- Testing and commissioning electrical installations;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical faults and malfunctions;
- Supporting upgrades and modifications of onboard systems.

You will mainly work at shipyards and port locations, with occasional assignments on board vessels.

- MBO-level education in Electrical Engineering or Maritime Technology;
- Experience with electrical installations, preferably in the maritime sector;
- Knowledge of maritime systems and standards is an advantage;
- VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B;
- Independent and accurate working style;
- Good command of Dutch or English.

As an Electrotechnician, you will play a key role in ensuring the reliability and safety of electrical systems. You will work on installation projects, perform maintenance activities, and troubleshoot technical issues to keep operations running smoothly.

Your daily responsibilities include:

- Installing electrical systems and equipment;
- Performing preventive and corrective maintenance;
- Diagnosing and resolving electrical faults and malfunctions;
- Inspecting installations to ensure compliance with safety regulations;
- Reading and interpreting technical drawings and electrical schematics;
- Collaborating with colleagues and customers to deliver high-quality solutions.

This is a varied position where no two days are the same, offering plenty of opportunities to further develop your technical skills.

- MBO Level 3 diploma in Electrical Engineering or a comparable technical qualification;
- Minimum of 2 years of experience as an Electrotechnician;
- Valid VCA certificate or willingness to obtain one;
- Driving license B is considered an advantage;
- Good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Strong focus on safety, quality, and precision;
- Ability to work independently as well as part of a team.
